=3 Notes
* The Periqia Pugils are scattered around the middle of the map, they are true sound.
* The Black Baron will spawn randomly in one of several locations around the map, either in the middle area or within the NW, NE, SW, or SE tunnels.

=2 Walkthrough
Shoot down The {m:Black Baron}.
* You will enter the Assault on the east side of the map in the room at (I-8). This is also where the {p:Rune of Release} spawns.
* The Black Baron will not appear on {p:Widescan}.
* A short time after he is engaged the Baron will warp away to a different part of the map. For this reason having a job that can summon a pet to follow him to his next location is extremely useful, as it will save a lot of time. /SMN is also fine for this. It should be noted that at ilvl 119 the {m:Black Baron} dies in one weaponskill. The pet strategy is no longer necessary.
* While he has significantly more HP, he is otherwise pretty much the same as a regular VT {p:Imp}.

